# Binary assets: mark so git applies no text/EOL filters and treats them as
# non-diffable blobs. Per CLAUDE.md's source-byte-law carve-out (M8-03), a path
# declared `binary` here is exempt from the printable-ASCII source-byte law and
# the per-artifact NUL/C0 scan. The scan still runs on every TEXT blob in the
# diff. apps/portfolio/.gitattributes (M8-03) declares `*.woff2 binary` for the
# portfolio font subset; this root file adds the M6-05 resume-render assets.
#
# Committed OFL font binaries embedded in the deterministic PDF export
# (packages/resume-render/src/fonts). OFL.txt beside them is plain-ASCII TEXT and
# is scanned normally.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# The M6-05 render goldens are ALL plain-ASCII TEXT (byte-golden .md/.txt/.json
# and CONTENT-golden resume.pdf.txt / resume.docx.txt) and are scanned normally -
# no byte-golden binary fixture exists, because the M6-05 spike found PDF (fontkit
# subset tables, V8 hash-seed ordering) and DOCX (zip wobble) are
# content-deterministic, not byte-deterministic. So no path-scoped binary golden
# entry is needed; only the embedded fonts above are declared binary.

# Shell hooks run via a shebang. A CRLF line ending makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter named "bash\r", the script exits 127, and since only exit 2
# blocks, the tool call PROCEEDS - a security hook that fails open on a
# checkout quirk. Force LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
